# Start: the systems page, focus on its first system row, NO SYSTEM TICKED
# (see run-transfer.steps for why). End: the CLOUD hub. Like run-transfer
# but a frame every three seconds for a minute, so every phase of a run
# with settings, saves and several systems is caught on the page (#95).
#
# This is the one file where `wait N` is still right, and it is not a guess
# about timing: the fixed waits here are a SAMPLER. The point is a frame at
# a known offset from the start of the transfer -- t+2 s, t+5 s, t+8 s --
# so the phases can be read off in order. A settle would wait for the page
# to stop moving, which is precisely what this file exists not to do. The
# presses before the transfer starts still use the frame steps, because
# those are waits for a screen and not samples of one.
key up
wait-for-change
key right
wait-for-change
key x
wait-for-change 15 0
settle
shot selected-all
key right
wait-for-change
key x
wait-for-change 25 0
shot t02
wait 3
shot t05
wait 3
shot t08
wait 3
shot t11
wait 3
shot t14
wait 3
shot t17
wait 3
shot t20
wait 3
shot t23
wait 3
shot t26
wait 3
shot t29
wait 3
shot t32
wait 4
shot t36
wait 4
shot t40
wait 5
shot t45
wait 5
shot t50
wait 10
shot t60
key x
wait-for-change 15
settle
